  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Is it true that a group satisfying Kazhdan’s property (T) cannot homomor-\nphically map onto infinitely many simple groups of Lie type of rank 1?\n   It is known that a group which maps onto P SL2 (q) for infinitely many q does not\nhave Kazhdan’s property (T).                                       A. Jaikin-Zapirain",
